 Print data;⎕IO;∆WSELF;t;cfg;pn;⎕ML
⍝∇ Davin's "Print" utility ⍝ ****  Direct ported from APL+Win to test with ∆WI  *****
⍝∇      Print <text> ...
⍝∇ Prints one or more text (or code) blocks to the printer.
⍝∇ Text items can be character arrays (⍴⍴≤2), or arrays of higher rank
⍝∇ (⍴⍴>2) where each plane of the array is printed on a separate page
⍝∇ of paper (it inserts ⎕TCFF codes between planes of the array).
⍝∇ Allowed special characters include: ⎕TCNL, ⎕TCLF, ⎕TCFF.
⍝∇ Numeric items may also be included and will be sent to the printer
⍝∇ without processing so that control codes and escape sequences can
⍝∇ be printed directly.  Interesting codes include: 13, 10, 12, 27.
⍝∇ The numeric code ¯1 may also be included to close the printer and
⍝∇ delete it's associated object from memory (if desired).  This also
⍝∇ causes the printer to flush its buffer and print any pending output.
⍝∇ The numeric code ¯2 may also be included to simply close and then
⍝∇ re-open the printer object.  This causes the printer to flush it's
⍝∇ buffers but leaves it open for further output (and leaves any
⍝∇ external definitions intact).
⍝∇ The numeric code ¯3 may also be included to abort the printing in
⍝∇ progress and cancel any output already sent to Print but not yet
⍝∇ "flushed".  The printer remains open.
⍝∇ The numeric code ¯4 may be included as a auxilary method of producing
⍝∇ a "form feed" or "new page" on the printer.  It is functionally identical
⍝∇ to the use of a 12 or ⎕TCFF code.
⍝∇ The printer object's properties may be modified by creating the printer
⍝∇ with "Print ''" and then modifying the printer object directly before
⍝∇ proceeding to use ∇Print for output.

 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←2
⍝ If called with multiple arguments, process them one at a time, then exit.
 :If 1<≡data ⋄ Print¨data ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf
⍝ If called with a 3-D matrix, print one on each page
 :If 2<⍴⍴data ⋄ Print¨,(⊂[1↓⍴data]data),[1.5]¯4 ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf

 :If 0=⎕NC pn←'Printer_Name' ⋄ pn←'Printer' ⋄ :Else ⋄ pn←⍎pn ⋄ :EndIf
 :If 0=⍴∆WSELF←pn ∆WI'self' ⍝ Does "Printer" need to be created?
     cfg←⊂'caption' 'APL Printer Object' ⍝ Typical configuration...
     cfg←cfg,⊂'font' 'APLPLUS' 1 0 'symbol'
     ∆WSELF←pn ∆WI'New' 'Printer',1↓cfg ⍝ Make it
 :Else ⋄ ('"',pn,'" is not a Printer!')⎕SIGNAL 11/⍨~'Printer'≡∆WI'class'
 :EndIf

⍝ Time to start printing...
 :If 1<⍴⍴data←1/data ⋄ data←,data,⎕UCS 13 ⋄ :EndIf
 :While ×⍴data
     :If 0<t←+/∧\data∊⎕AV~⎕UCS 12 ⍝ Find "normal" characters
         ∆WI'Print'(t↑data) ⍝ Print them
     :EndIf
     :If ×⍴data←t↓data ⍝ Anything left over?
         :Select ↑data ⍝ What's the first item look like?
         :CaseList (⎕UCS 12)12 ¯4 ⍝ Is it a formfeed?
             ∆WI'Eject' ⋄ data←1↓data ⍝ Do it the built-in way
         :Case ¯1 ⍝ Special code -- Close/Delete Printer = *Done*
             :If ∆WI'Close' ⋄ 0 0⍴'⎕wgive 0' ⋄ ∆WI'Delete' ⋄ data←1↓data
             :Else ⋄ 11 ⎕SIGNAL⍨'Printer "',pn,'" close failure!'
             :EndIf
             :If ×⍴data ⍝ If there's anything else left...
                 Print data ⋄ data←'' ⍝ We must recurse to print it
             :EndIf
         :Case ¯2 ⍝ Special code -- Close/Open Printer
             :If ∆WI'Close' ⋄ ∆WI'Open' ⋄ data←1↓data
             :Else ⋄ 11 ⎕SIGNAL⍨'"Printer" close failure!'
             :EndIf ⍝ Now we may continue
         :Case ¯3 ⍝ Special code -- Abort printing in progress
             ∆WI'Abort' ⋄ data←1↓data ⍝ Just "can" it
         :Else ⍝ Anything else better be just ⎕AF number(s)
             t←+/∧\0=↑0⍴⊂data ⋄ t←t⌊¯1+(t↑data)⍳¯1
             ∆WI'Print'(⎕AV[t↑data]) ⋄ data←t↓data ⍝ Send it
         :EndSelect
     :EndIf
 :EndWhile ⍝ And continue until we run out of stuff to print
⍝ That's all, folks!
